1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,437
This video shows Omnichannel Addresses, the list of phone numbers your business owns:

2
00:00:06,437 --> 00:00:10,321
what each is used for, how to add one, which agents call or

3
00:00:10,321 --> 00:00:13,070
text from it, and how to clone a number.

4
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:20,814
Your business owns numbers, and each has a job.

5
00:00:20,814 --> 00:00:25,619
Agents dial out from them, automatic texts are sent from them, and incoming

6
00:00:25,619 --> 00:00:28,110
calls and texts are matched to them.

7
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:34,062
Each address is listed once, with a checkbox for each thing it is used for:

8
00:00:34,062 --> 00:00:36,760
voice calls, text messages, or both.

9
00:00:37,510 --> 00:00:41,524
So you manage a number in one place, and every feature that needs

10
00:00:41,524 --> 00:00:43,560
a number picks from this list.

11
00:00:47,769 --> 00:00:52,379
Open Interaction Center, Management, Omnichannel Addresses.

12
00:00:52,379 --> 00:00:57,060
Each row is an address, with badges for its kind, what it is

13
00:00:57,060 --> 00:01:00,535
used for, its number, and its SMS provider.

14
00:01:00,535 --> 00:01:05,429
Here, one number is for calls, and another for calls and texts.

15
00:01:09,629 --> 00:01:13,639
Click Add Address, and pick the kind, such as a phone number.

16
00:01:13,639 --> 00:01:17,529
Only kinds that something on your site can use are offered.

17
00:01:17,529 --> 00:01:21,420
If none is, the page asks you to enable a feature that uses

18
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:25,489
addresses, like Contact Center Voice or SMS Messaging Channel.

19
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:31,383
Enter a name people will recognize, and the number in international format.

20
00:01:31,383 --> 00:01:35,079
Under Used for, tick what the number is used for.

21
00:01:35,079 --> 00:01:41,933
Voice calls appears with Contact Center Voice, and Text messages with the SMS Messaging Channel.

22
00:01:41,933 --> 00:01:43,680
Here, text messages.

23
00:01:44,131 --> 00:01:47,624
The settings for each use appear while it is ticked.

24
00:01:47,624 --> 00:01:52,260
For text messages, pick the SMS provider that owns the number, or leave

25
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:56,415
it on the tenant default, and pick the agents who text from it.

26
00:01:56,415 --> 00:01:58,763
Each agent texts from one number.

27
00:01:58,763 --> 00:02:01,171
Add a description, and click Save.

28
00:02:05,374 --> 00:02:09,612
To add a number set up like an existing one, open the address's

29
00:02:09,612 --> 00:02:11,823
Actions menu and choose Clone.

30
00:02:11,823 --> 00:02:16,245
The form opens with the kind, what it is used for, the description

31
00:02:16,245 --> 00:02:17,904
and the SMS provider.

32
00:02:18,356 --> 00:02:21,726
Enter the new number and a name, and click Save.

33
00:02:21,726 --> 00:02:26,469
The number and its agents are not copied, because each agent dials and

34
00:02:26,469 --> 00:02:28,216
texts from one number.

35
00:02:32,416 --> 00:02:36,857
For voice calls, you also pick the agents who dial from the number.

36
00:02:36,857 --> 00:02:42,636
Agents on no number's list use the default numbers chosen under Settings, Contact Center.

37
00:02:43,386 --> 00:02:46,884
The number a customer sees is the first that applies:

38
00:02:46,884 --> 00:02:51,863
the load's Dial from number, the agent's own line, the dialer profile's caller

39
00:02:51,863 --> 00:02:54,116
ID, then the provider's default.

40
00:02:54,866 --> 00:03:00,588
Which entry point answers a number's calls or texts is set on the entry point.

41
00:03:00,588 --> 00:03:05,424
An address is never deleted, and a number is listed once, so tick

42
00:03:05,424 --> 00:03:07,876
both uses on the same address.

43
00:03:12,076 --> 00:03:15,576
List every number the business owns in one place.

44
00:03:16,326 --> 00:03:19,736
Give each agent the number they call or text from.

45
00:03:20,486 --> 00:03:24,106
Choose the number an automatic text campaign sends from.

46
00:03:24,856 --> 00:03:28,386
Clone a number to set up a new line in seconds.

47
00:03:30,386 --> 00:03:34,107
Keep one address for each number, tick what it is used for, and

48
00:03:34,107 --> 00:03:35,995
assign the agents who use it.

49
00:03:35,995 --> 00:03:40,094
The user manual and the technical guide are linked in the description.

50
00:03:40,094 --> 00:03:41,496
Thanks for watching.

